---
// `form` — a contact / inquiry form: an optional lead (intro), then one field per `### <label>`
// (parsed in site-core.js: a trailing `{email}`/`{tel}`/`{textarea}` sets the input kind, `- option`
// lines under a field become a <select>). Renders a native <form> with <label> + <input>/<textarea>/
// <select> per field + a submit button; the THEME paints `.st-form-*`. This coral carries only
// STRUCTURE — the `action`/`method` params wire submission (a deploy concern, per
// cutover-structure-before-data); with no action the submit button renders DISABLED — 🩸 it used
// to render live and post to the page's own URL, which on a static host is a 405 the visitor never
// sees (measured on a customer's site, 2026-08-15). "Never claims a backend it lacks" was in this comment
// before it was in the markup. `action=inbox` is the one special value — a fixed, wired route to
// feelreef's own same-origin inbox forwarder; see the note below. Family posture: CommonMark, one `%% sitetile: %%` sentinel, native elements,
// zero-JS, GAIDO-editable (fields live in the Markdown). A near-universal contact widget no other
// coral expresses — grown when a real /contact page hit the wall (recast doctrine: hit a wall,
// grow a GENERAL coral).
// The markup is packages/emit/form.mjs (tile-lab#52); this component reads the params, resolves
// what only a build knows (its own path, the locale home, the thanks manifest) and hands it over.
import { parseParams, inlineHtml, bodyHtml, safeHref, safeInternalPath } from '@sitetile';
import { emitForm } from '@emit/form.mjs';
import { inboxFormCopy, DEFAULT_LANG, localeHomePath, contentRelsOf } from '../../packages/lingo/locale.mjs';
import { recordThanks } from '../../../noindex-pass.mjs';
const { section, index = 0, hero, lang, meta } = Astro.props;
const pm = parseParams(section.params);
// `eyebrow="…"` — the small label above the heading, the same seam every other
// heading-bearing coral now has. 🩸 Three had it and six did not, with nothing in the
// grammar explaining the split; authors reasonably used it everywhere and it silently
// did nothing. Absent → no DOM change.
const eyebrow = pm.eyebrow ? (typeof pm.eyebrow === 'object' ? pm.eyebrow.label : pm.eyebrow) : null;
const submit = pm.submit || 'Send';

// ── 🩸 `inbox=` IS BACK, 2026-09-03 — the same-origin route it needed exists now ──
//
// It first shipped on 2026-08-15 and was withdrawn the same day: the idea then was
// one param pointing the form straight at feelreef's `/api/inbox`, cross-origin.
// That cannot work — feelreef is a SvelteKit app, and SvelteKit refuses any
// cross-origin POST whose content type is a FORM type, app-wide, before routing
// (`Cross-site POST form submissions are forbidden` — the same check that protects
// the dashboard's reply/claim actions, signup, checkout, the pay links). No enctype
// a browser sends for a plain `<form>` dodges it.
//
// The withdrawal note said the fix was a SAME-ORIGIN route: the form posts to the
// site's own path and the site's emitted `_worker.js` forwards it server-to-server.
// That forwarder now exists on the reef side, so this coral's half is just wiring
// `action=inbox` to it — a fixed, non-configurable contract:
//
//   • `action=inbox` → `<form action="/__reef/inbox" method="post">`. `method=` is
//     ignored for this value — the forwarder only accepts POST.
//   • Hidden inputs the forwarder reads: `return_to` (this page's own path,
//     locale-aware — Astro.url.pathname already carries the locale segment), an
//     opt-in `thanks_to` (see `thanks=`, below), `return_fragment` (the JSON
//     outcome-to-fragment map for this form), and a honeypot `_hp` (visually
//     hidden, NOT `display:none`, so a bot's autofill still reaches it — a
//     display:none field is exactly what a scripted filler is taught to skip;
//     kept out of the tab order and off-screen instead).
//   • No `kind`/`id` param here — the forwarder bakes the site key server-side. This
//     coral still carries only STRUCTURE, per cutover-structure-before-data.
//   • Field naming: the `{email}` field is posted as `visitor_email` (the forwarder's
//     one semantic field — it composes every other field into the message body under
//     its own visible label). A label that collides with one of the forwarder's
//     reserved names gets `field_` prefixed on the WIRE name only — the visible
//     `<label>` text an author wrote never changes.
//
// 🔴 Do not re-add a version of this that posts straight to feelreef.com. It will
// look correct in every test that calls the endpoint directly, and fail for every
// real visitor — that is the exact failure this route exists to avoid.
//
// ── `thanks=<path>` — an editable page instead of the built-in card ──
//
// `action=inbox`'s built-in success card is a fixed sentence this coral writes; some owners
// want their own page instead — one they can edit like any other, with their own copy and their
// own tracking snippet. `thanks=/some/page` names it: on a successful submit the forwarder 303s
// there (with `?inbox=sent` appended, an existing query string preserved) instead of back to
// this page. A FAILED submit is unaffected — it still returns HERE with `?inbox=<outcome>`, so
// the inline retry error above the button keeps working exactly as it does without `thanks=`.
//
// Validated with `safeInternalPath` — the same allowlist family as `safeHref`/`action=` above,
// but stricter: it must be a path ON THIS SITE (`/…`, no scheme, no `//`, no `..`), never an
// off-site destination — see safeInternalPath's own comment in site-core.js. An invalid value is
// dropped (recorded via `takeDropWarnings`, same diagnostics queue every other gated destination
// in this file already uses) and never reaches the DOM: no hidden field, `formAction`/the
// built-in success card and everything else render exactly as if `thanks=` had not been written.
//
// Carried to the forwarder as a hidden `thanks_to` field, NOT trusted as-is once there — a hidden
// input is still something a visitor's own browser tooling can edit before the request leaves it,
// so the forwarder re-validates whatever arrives on the wire with the same internal-path rule
// before it is ever allowed to become a redirect target (see shop-function-template.js).
const action = pm.action || undefined;
const isInbox = action === 'inbox';
const method = isInbox ? 'post' : (pm.method || 'post').toLowerCase();
// round 4 (R3-P2-1): `action=` is a raw author-controlled destination reaching a live
// `<form action>` — gate it here, at the value's one declaration point, the same shape every
// other Astro consumer of safeHref/safeSrc already uses. A disallowed scheme (e.g.
// `action="javascript:…"`) degrades to `undefined`, which is `wired`'s existing "no backend"
// path below — the same disabled-submit degradation an absent `action=` already gets.
const formAction = isInbox ? '/__reef/inbox' : (safeHref(action) || undefined);
// Validated regardless of `action=` (an author gets the same build-time feedback either way —
// see safeInternalPath's own comment), but only ever WIRED (rendered as a hidden field, used by
// the copy the script reads) when `isInbox` — `thanks=` is meaningless outside the one route that
// can act on it.
const thanksPath = safeInternalPath(pm.thanks);
// reef#2554: a thanks page is noindex by default. This form is the one place that knows a
// `thanks_to` is ours, so it records the target in the build's thanks manifest and marks itself
// with the id; the post-build pass (noindex-pass.mjs) counts the entry only if that id reached an
// emitted file, then removes the mark. Not recorded outside a build: no attribute at all.
const thanksMark = isInbox && thanksPath ? recordThanks(thanksPath) : undefined;

// The forwarder's reserved field names (an owner field never lands on the wire under one) and
// the `field_` prefix that avoids them live with the field markup, in emitForm.
// `return_to` — locale-aware because Astro.url.pathname IS the built path, which
// already carries the locale segment for every non-default-locale page (the router
// bakes it in via toUrlLocale; see lib routing). Read once, per page render.
const returnTo = Astro.url.pathname;
// "Back to homepage" on the success card — the home of the locale `returnTo` sits under, from the
// same built path and through the same function the header logo uses (lingo/locale.mjs →
// localeHomePath). 🩸 reef#1891: it was a literal `/`, one line below a link that carried
// the locale, so a zh-TW visitor was handed back to the English home. MEASURED against the content
// files: a locale with a contact page and no home content file yet keeps `/` rather than a prefix
// whose home was never written (content file present = counted, as hreflang counts it).
// No `meta` (a caller that renders this coral without the site config) → no locales → `/`.
const homeHref = isInbox ? localeHomePath({
  locales: meta && meta.locales,
  pathname: returnTo,
  contentRels: contentRelsOf(import.meta.glob('../../../content/**/*.md', { query: '?raw', import: 'default', eager: true })),
}) : '/';

// 🔴 A form with nowhere to send is not a form with a working button: emitForm renders the submit
// DISABLED unless `formAction` is set (round 4: gated on `formAction`, not the raw `action` — a
// hostile action disables the button, it does not merely swap what it posts to).
//
// Required fields, the success sentence and the `data-inbox-copy` payload the script reads are
// worked out in emitForm from the fields and this locale's copy below (2026-09-03 cold-read
// findings #9/#10; owner ruling on the success card).
const fieldCopy = inboxFormCopy(lang || DEFAULT_LANG);

---
<Fragment set:html={emitForm(section, { eyebrow, submit, isInbox, formAction, method, thanksPath, thanksMark, returnTo, homeHref, copy: fieldCopy }, { hero, index, inline: inlineHtml, block: bodyHtml })} />
